-- title:
--   Oriented crossing charts uv=q^e on the Deligne–Rapoport model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, i.e. the bundle of data and properties for the model `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` of level $N_0q$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `DRLevel.R q`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O\colon$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to\kappa$ a ring map. Write $X_O$ for the pullback of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$. Let $\mathrm{bc}$ be a morphism from `DRLevel.fibre (toκ.comp ρO)`, the pullback along $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O)$, to $X_O$ which is compatible with both projections, the second up to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$. Points of the fibre product of the two component morphisms `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 1` of the package are called crossings; for such a point $n$ let $x_n\in X_O$ be the image of $n$ under the first projection, followed by `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and $\mathrm{bc}$. Assume (hypothesis `hrat`) that every such $x_n$ is the image of the closed point under some section $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field of $O$ $\to X_O$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map. The conclusion asserts: for every crossing $n$ there are an integer $e\ge 1$, an open $U\subseteq X_O$ containing $x_n$, and a morphism $f\colon U\to\operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[u,v]/(uv-q^e)\bigr)$ (the scheme `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme` of $q^e$ over $O$) such that: $f$ followed by the structure map $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $O[u,v]/(uv-q^e)\to\operatorname{Spec} O$ agrees with the inclusion $U\hookrightarrow X_O$ followed by the second projection; a point $y\in U$ has both `CrossingQuotient.U` and `CrossingQuotient.V` (the classes of $u$ and $v$) in the prime $f(y)$ precisely when $y$ maps to $x_n$; at every $y$ over $x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism of residue fields; and, in both directions, $v\in f(y)$ holds exactly when $y$ lies in the image of `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` followed by $\mathrm{bc}$, while $u\in f(y)$ holds exactly when $y$ lies in the image of `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 1` followed by $\mathrm{bc}$.
--
--   This is the local description of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ at a crossing point of its fibre at $q$: an oriented chart $uv=q^e$, formally étale at the point over the base $O$, in which the two branches through the crossing are matched with the two components of the geometric fibre in a prescribed order. It is used in the construction of a resolved model package with the prescribed node data, via [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_nodeEquiv_swap_nodeCoordinates_of_surjective_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_nodeEquiv_swap_nodeCoordinates_of_surjective_of_sp_eq_spPlace).
